      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Char the onion halves and ginger directly over a gas flame or under a very hot grill until blackened in places. About 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place the whole chicken in a stockpot. Cover with 2.5 litres of cold water. Bring to the boil and skim thoroughly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the charred onion, ginger, and star anise. Reduce to a very gentle simmer. Poach for 45 to 55 minutes until the chicken is cooked through."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the chicken and cool slightly. Strain the broth and return to the pot. Season with fish sauce and sugar."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pull or slice the chicken meat off the bones. Discard the skin and bones."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fry the sliced shallots in oil over medium heat until deep golden and crispy. Drain on kitchen paper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the soaked glass noodles between 4 bowls. Add the wood ear mushrooms. Ladle the very hot broth over the noodles . the heat of the broth will cook the noodles in the bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Top each bowl with shredded chicken, spring onion, coriander, and crispy fried shallots. Serve with lime and chilli on the side."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The glass noodles clump into a solid mass in the bowl.",
              "cause": "They were not soaked long enough or were added too dry.",
              "fix": "Soak in cold water for 20 minutes until fully softened. Separate the strands and loosen with your fingers before placing in the bowl."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The wood ear mushrooms are still hard and rubbery.",
              "cause": "They were not soaked for long enough.",
              "fix": "Dried wood ear mushrooms need at least 20 minutes in warm water to fully rehydrate. Squeeze and rinse before slicing."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The broth tastes flat and lacks depth.",
              "cause": "The onion and ginger were not charred enough.",
              "fix": "The charring step is essential. Char until the outside is quite blackened - this gives the broth its sweetness and colour."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Miến gà is eaten throughout Vietnam and is especially loved as a restorative meal. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Vietnamese families make it when someone is unwell or recovering from illness. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The clear broth and gentle noodles are considered easy to digest and comforting. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is also a common dish served at funeral meals and post-ceremony gatherings in northern Vietnam. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Despite its humble reputation, a well-made miến gà with crispy shallots is very good."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
